#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114899 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7e817a0-edcf-54ca-ba4c-ffe91af04675" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Height of a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "972fe403-9a15-5d10-8f9f-f5c93eb586ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-2725" :question/problem "Given $\\triangle{ABC}$ above, which of the following diagrams represents the height corresponding to $\\overline{BC}$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1644/Source/Images/87a75efd5d2ea35b34a69e706f1be627.png)" :question/worked-solution "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overline{BC}$ is a line segment that\n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $A$ to the line $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC}$, and\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC}$.\n\nThe correct diagram is shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1644/Source/Images/fd5ace30e6439ad0ec04323dff64158d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114900 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a76efbd-cefd-5aa0-953e-8ab50bec7ae0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Height Corresponding to an Extended Base"}] :question/id #uuid "2e6213d0-702f-5795-a99a-0051790c4e6d" :question/math-academy-id "e-2730" :question/problem "Consider the triangle $ABC$ shown below. Construct the height corresponding to $\\overline{BC}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1644/Source/Images/d58c024ed36386179c03f934732a521e.png)" :question/worked-solution "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overline{BC}$ is a line segment that\n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $A$ to the line $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC}$, and\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC}$.\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overline{BC}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1644/Source/Images/5984daacf17d0df2c5d1243d331fed62.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $A$ to $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1644/Source/Images/cec2c1f0447854e20eb91aa386433b58.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115077 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a916099-a237-5612-b7f1-3679b7ff069d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "43c770ec-d353-5e9e-b44e-f06417dab2ab" :question/math-academy-id "e-9731" :question/problem "Consider $\\triangle ABC$ shown above. The line segment $\\overline{CH}$ is the altitude corresponding to $\\overline{AB}$. If $m\\angle BAC = 115^\\circ$, calculate $m\\angle HCA$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1644/Source/Images/a71ef168add2cbe0cc9e0e59be1c952d.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since the straight angle must have a measure of $180^\\circ$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠HAC + m∠BAC &= 180^{∘} \\\\\nm∠HAC + 115^{∘} &= 180^{∘} \\\\\nm∠HAC &= 65^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\triangle ACH$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to $180^\\circ$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠HCA + m∠HAC + m∠AHC &= 180^{∘} \\\\\nm∠HCA + 65^{∘} + 90^{∘} &= 180^{∘} \\\\\nm∠HCA + 155^{∘} &= 180^{∘} \\\\\nm∠HCA &= 25^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115566 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a76efbd-cefd-5aa0-953e-8ab50bec7ae0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Height Corresponding to an Extended Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a679694e-fe3a-5eb0-ba27-fb70e0b6d91f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1644/Source/Images/q-27666-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112797} {:answer/id #uuid "db7fc2fd-f3d6-506b-839b-f14b9bc3d300" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1644/Source/Images/q-27666-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112798} {:answer/id #uuid "02e76b47-7c6f-5396-8cec-5192ce5d2e59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image}